### Edit 3 — `src/util/jitter.ts:85-185`, replace both functions wholesale with:

```ts
function fixJitterAvoidOverlaps(
    fixedAxis: Axis2D | SingleAxis,
    fixedCoord: number,
    floatCoord: number,
    radius: number,
    jitter: number,
    margin: number,
    bandWidth: number | null
): number {
    const store = inner(fixedAxis);
    const items = store.items || (store.items = []);

    // The point is only allowed to move within
    // [floatCoord - maxMove, floatCoord + maxMove].
    let maxMove = jitter / 2;
    // Clamp only category axis.
    if (bandWidth) {
        maxMove = Math.min(maxMove, bandWidth / 2 - radius);
    }

    let resultCoord: number = null;

    if (maxMove >= 0) {
        // The new point overlaps an existing item if and only if its floatCoord
        // falls into the open interval (item.floatCoord ± halfSpan). Collect all
        // such forbidden intervals, then pick the nearest position outside them.
        const forbidden: number[][] = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            const item = items[i];
            const dx = fixedCoord - item.fixedCoord;
            const r = radius + item.r + margin;
            const halfSpanSquare = r * r - dx * dx;
            if (halfSpanSquare > 0) {
                const halfSpan = Math.sqrt(halfSpanSquare);
                const lower = item.floatCoord - halfSpan;
                const upper = item.floatCoord + halfSpan;
                // Ignore the intervals that can't cover the movable range.
                if (upper > floatCoord - maxMove && lower < floatCoord + maxMove) {
                    forbidden.push([lower, upper]);
                }
            }
        }
        resultCoord = findNearestFreeCoord(forbidden, floatCoord, maxMove);
    }

    if (resultCoord == null) {
        // The movable range is genuinely exhausted. Fall back to random jitter.
        resultCoord = fixJitterIgnoreOverlaps(floatCoord, jitter, bandWidth, radius);
    }

    // Insert to store. Note that the stored coord must be the coord that is
    // actually used, otherwise the following points are tested against a
    // position that is not rendered.
    items.push({
        fixedCoord: fixedCoord,
        floatCoord: resultCoord,
        r: radius
    });

    return resultCoord;
}

/**
 * Find the coord nearest to `floatCoord` that is inside
 * [floatCoord - maxMove, floatCoord + maxMove] and outside every `forbidden`
 * open interval. Returns null only if no such coord exists.
 */
function findNearestFreeCoord(
    forbidden: number[][],
    floatCoord: number,
    maxMove: number
): number {
    if (!forbidden.length) {
        return floatCoord;
    }
    forbidden.sort(function (a, b) {
        return a[0] - b[0];
    });

    // Merge into maximal disjoint intervals, so that the bounds of every merged
    // interval are guaranteed to be free positions (tangent, not overlapping).
    const merged: number[][] = [[forbidden[0][0], forbidden[0][1]]];
    for (let i = 1; i < forbidden.length; i++) {
        const last = merged[merged.length - 1];
        if (forbidden[i][0] <= last[1]) {
            last[1] = Math.max(last[1], forbidden[i][1]);
        }
        else {
            merged.push([forbidden[i][0], forbidden[i][1]]);
        }
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < merged.length; i++) {
        const lower = merged[i][0];
        const upper = merged[i][1];
        if (floatCoord <= lower) {
            // Not covered by this or any following interval.
            return floatCoord;
        }
        if (floatCoord < upper) {
            // Covered. The nearest free positions are the two bounds.
            const useLower = floatCoord - lower <= upper - floatCoord;
            const nearer = useLower ? lower : upper;
            const farther = useLower ? upper : lower;
            if (Math.abs(nearer - floatCoord) <= maxMove) {
                return nearer;
            }
            return Math.abs(farther - floatCoord) <= maxMove ? farther : null;
        }
    }
    return floatCoord;
}
```

Why the merge bounds are safe: overlap is a strict test (`d2 < r * r`), so a position exactly `h` away from a blocker's center is tangent, not overlapping. Merging with `<=` guarantees `merged[i][1] < merged[i + 1][0]` strictly, so each merged bound is outside every merged interval — no O(k²) re-verification is needed. Complexity is O(k log k) per point (vs. the old O(k)), with k = number of already-placed points that can block; overall still O(n²)-ish, same order as before.

Note on the range pre-filter: dropping intervals that don't intersect the closed movable range cannot make an in-range bound spuriously "free", since a dropped interval contains no in-range point.

Imports at `src/util/jitter.ts:1-6` all stay used (`Axis2D` for the `instanceof`, `makeInner`, `AxisBaseModel`, `SingleAxis`, `Axis`, `SeriesModel`). No import changes.

## Tests

No unit tests currently reference jitter (`grep -ril jitter test/ut/` returns nothing). Visual-only coverage exists at `/workspace/test/scatter-jitter.html` (cartesian category + singleAxis cases, `jitterOverlap: true/false`, `jitter: 20/50/150/200/400/500`) and `/workspace/test/violin.html`.

Add `/workspace/test/ut/spec/util/jitter.test.ts` — `test/ut/jest.config.cjs` `testMatch` already includes `'**/spec/util/*.test.ts'`, so it is picked up by `npm test` with no config change. Import via the `@/src/...` alias, as in `test/ut/spec/util/number.test.ts`:

```ts
import { fixJitter } from '@/src/util/jitter';
```

`fixJitter` can be driven with a plain mock cast to `any`, because (a) the `instanceof Axis2D` guard at line 45 is skipped for non-`Axis2D` objects, and (b) `makeInner` (`src/util/model.ts:737-742`) just stashes a property on the host object, so any object works as the per-axis store key:

```ts
function createAxis(opt: any) {
    return {
        scale: { type: opt.scaleType || 'ordinal' },
        getBandWidth: () => opt.bandWidth,
        model: { get: (key: string) => opt[key] }
    } as any;
}
```

Cases worth asserting:
- Two points at the same `fixedCoord`, `floatCoord` 100 and 105, `radius` 5, `margin` 0, `jitter` 100 → second result must satisfy `|result - 100| >= 10` (no overlap) and `|result - 105| <= 50` (inside budget). The old code passes this trivially; use 3+ points to hit the ordering bug.
- The ordering regression: place blockers at 118 then 100 (insert in that order), then a point at 105 → old code returns 110 (overlapping 118), new code must return 128.
- Determinism: with enough free space the result must be reproducible (no `Math.random`); stub `Math.random` to a constant to detect an unwanted fallback.
- Genuinely exhausted case: many points at the same `fixedCoord` with `jitter` small enough that no free slot exists → fallback still stays within the band.
- Single axis (`bandWidth` null / `scaleType` not `'ordinal'`) → no band clamp applied.

## 1. How axis labels/ticks are actually built

Entry point: `Axis#getViewLabels()` → `createAxisLabels()`.

`src/coord/Axis.ts:242-247`
```ts
    getViewLabels(
        ctx?: AxisLabelsComputingContext
    ): ReturnType<typeof createAxisLabels>['labels'] {
        ctx = ctx || createAxisLabelsComputingContext(AxisTickLabelComputingKind.determine);
        return createAxisLabels(this, ctx).labels;
    }
```
Consumers of `getViewLabels()`: `src/component/axis/AxisBuilder.ts:1352`, `src/component/axis/AngleAxisView.ts:100`, `src/component/timeline/SliderTimelineView.ts:468`, `src/chart/line/LineView.ts:409`. They only read `labelItem.formattedLabel` / `rawLabel` / `tickValue`, so none of them need changing.

`createAxisLabels` has exactly three branches (`src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:123-149`):

* **`axisLabel.customValues` branch (all axis types)** — lines 126-144, builds labels itself from the parsed custom values.
* **category** → `makeCategoryLabels` → `makeCategoryLabelsActually` → `makeLabelsByNumericCategoryInterval` (line 475) or `makeLabelsByCustomizedCategoryInterval` (line 551).
* **value / log / time** → `makeRealNumberLabels` (line 277), which maps over `axis.scale.getTicks()`.

`createAxisTicks` (line 154) has the parallel `axisTick.customValues` branch but never invokes a formatter — no change needed there.

## 2. Every `labelFormatter(...)` invocation and whether it passes the index

`makeLabelFormatter` is defined at `src/coord/axisHelper.ts:239` with signature `(tick: ScaleTick, idx?: number) => string` (idx already optional, so no type change is required to start passing it).

| site | code | passes idx? |
|---|---|---|
| `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:136` | `formattedLabel: labelFormatter(tick),` | **NO — this is the bug** |
| `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:283` | `formattedLabel: labelFormatter(tick, idx),` | yes |
| `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:388` | `labelFormatter({ value: tickValue }), params.font, 'center', 'top'` | no (category-only size estimation; formatter ignores idx — leave as is) |
| `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:535` | `formattedLabel: labelFormatter(tickObj),` | no (category-only; see §4) |
| `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:575` | `formattedLabel: labelFormatter(tick),` | no (category-only; see §4) |
| `src/coord/cartesian/legacyContainLabel.ts:80` | `const label = labelFormatter(tick, i);` | yes |

Why only site 136 is functionally broken: inside `makeLabelFormatter`,
* the **category** branch (`axisHelper.ts:258-272`) *ignores* the passed `idx` and computes `tick.value - axis.scale.getExtent()[0]` instead (deliberate back-compat, see the comment at lines 260-265), so category axes already get a defined `index`;
* the **value/log** branch (`axisHelper.ts:273-287`) forwards the `idx` argument straight through as the 2nd formatter arg;
* the **time** branch (`axisHelper.ts:242-247`) forwards `idx` into `(axis.scale as TimeScale).getFormattedLabel(tick, idx, parsed)` → `src/scale/Time.ts:141-149` → `leveledFormat(tick, idx, ...)` at `src/util/time.ts:331-352`, where `template = formatter(tick.value, idx, extra)`.

So with `axisLabel.customValues` on a `value` / `log` / `time` axis, a function `formatter` receives `index === undefined`.

## 3. Required change — `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts`

EXACT current code, `src/coord/axisTickLabelBuilder.ts:123-149`:
```ts
export function createAxisLabels(axis: Axis, ctx: AxisLabelsComputingContext): {
    labels: AxisLabelInfoDetermined[]
} {
    const custom = axis.getLabelModel().get('customValues');
    if (custom) {
        const labelFormatter = makeLabelFormatter(axis);
        const extent = axis.scale.getExtent();
        const tickNumbers = tickValuesToNumbers(axis, custom);
        const ticks = zrUtil.filter(tickNumbers, val => val >= extent[0] && val <= extent[1]);
        return {
            labels: zrUtil.map(ticks, numval => {
                const tick = {value: numval};
                return {
                    formattedLabel: labelFormatter(tick),
                    rawLabel: axis.scale.getLabel(tick),
                    tickValue: numval,
                    time: undefined as ScaleTick['time'] | NullUndefined,
                    break: undefined as VisualAxisBreak | NullUndefined,
                };
            }),
        };
    }
```

EXACT replacement (only the two lines 133 and 136 change):
```ts
