## Why this is sufficient (no other call site needs touching)

- `toggleHoverEmphasis(itemGroup, ...)` at line 262 → `enableHoverEmphasis` → `traverseUpdateState(el, setDefaultStateProxy)` (`src/util/states.ts:762-767`) already installs `elementStateProxy` on every descendant, including the symbol paths, so the newly-populated `blur`/`select` state objects are picked up. It runs *after* the `eachChild` loop, which is fine — `setDefaultStateProxy` only assigns `el.stateProxy`.
- `ensureState` is idempotent; the existing `polygon.ensureState(stateName).ignore` loop at lines 209-214 is unaffected and order-independent w.r.t. line 202.
- `useStyle` (zrender `Displayable.ts:412-423`) does not clear `states`, so the ordering of `useStyle` vs. state assignment inside the loop does not matter.
- No changes to `src/chart/radar/RadarSeries.ts`: `RadarSeriesStateOption` already declares `itemStyle?: ItemStyleOption` (line 54), and `StatesOptionMixin` (`src/util/types.ts:1817-1851`) already exposes `blur?: StateOption & StatesMixin['blur']` and `select?: ...`, with `StatesMixinBase` (`:1811-1815`) supplying the optional `blur`/`select` keys that `RadarStatesMixin` omits. So `blur.itemStyle` / `select.itemStyle` are already valid, typed options — only the view ignored them.

## Summary of the defects found

Four different "margin geometries" coexist today:

1. `labelLayoutHelper.prepareLabelLayoutInfo` applies `textMargin` to the **local** rect but `minMargin` to the **global** rect — so `minMargin` is silently dropped from the OBB (`obb` is built from `localRect`+`transform`), i.e. rotated labels lose `minMargin` in `hideOverlap`/`labelIntersect`.
2. `chart/pie/labelLayout.ts` reads `label.style.margin` as a raw number in two places. With `textMargin` (array) this evaluates to a string concat → `NaN` → every outer pie label ends up hidden. It also inflates only the height, and calls `getBoundingRect()` before `getComputedTransform()` (opposite of the documented order).
3. `shiftLayoutOnX/Y` move `label.x/y` and `rect`, but leave `localRect`/`transform`/`obb` stale, so the `hideOverlap` that runs right after in `LabelManager.layout` uses pre-shift OBBs. The same staleness exists after `adjustBreakLabelPair` moves break labels.
4. `labelStyle.ts` lets the internal `opt.defaultTextMargin` override an explicit user `minMargin` (this makes `axis.nameTextStyle.minMargin` a complete no-op today).

