GOAL: add a new accepted value `'tangential-noflip'` for pie `label.rotate` that produces the tangential rotation **without** the conditional 180-degree flip that `'tangential'` applies on the lower half.

=====================================================================
1) HOW THE CURRENT CODE WORKS (read this before editing)
=====================================================================

Angle convention (src/chart/pie/pieLayout.ts, no edits needed there):
- src/chart/pie/pieLayout.ts:30 `const RADIAN = Math.PI / 180;`
- src/chart/pie/pieLayout.ts:44 `let startAngle = -seriesModel.get('startAngle') * RADIAN;`
- src/chart/pie/pieLayout.ts:48 `endAngle = endAngle === 'auto' ? startAngle - PI2 : -endAngle * RADIAN;`
- src/chart/pie/pieLayout.ts:72 `const dir = clockwise ? 1 : -1;`
Defaults (src/chart/pie/PieSeries.ts:220-222): `clockwise: true, startAngle: 90, endAngle: 'auto'`. So layout `startAngle = -PI/2` (12 o'clock, since screen y grows downward: nx = cos(theta), ny = sin(theta), ny > 0 means below the center) and angles increase clockwise on screen. pieLayout.ts stores `startAngle`/`endAngle` per item; labelLayout derives `midAngle` from the sector shape.

The only place pie reads `label.rotate` is src/chart/pie/labelLayout.ts:466-497 (inside the `data.each(function (idx) {...})` body that starts at line 374). Exact current text:

```
466|        const PI = Math.PI;
467|        let labelRotate = 0;
468|        const rotate = labelModel.get('rotate');
469|        if (isNumber(rotate)) {
470|            labelRotate = rotate * (PI / 180);
471|        }
472|        else if (labelPosition === 'center') {
473|            labelRotate = 0;
474|        }
475|        else if (rotate === 'radial' || rotate === true) {
476|            const radialAngle = nx < 0 ? -midAngle + PI : -midAngle;
477|            labelRotate = radialAngle;
478|        }
479|        else if (rotate === 'tangential'
480|            && labelPosition !== 'outside' && labelPosition !== 'outer'
481|        ) {
482|            let rad = Math.atan2(nx, ny);
483|            if (rad < 0) {
484|                rad = PI * 2 + rad;
485|            }
486|            const isDown = ny > 0;
487|            if (isDown) {
488|                rad = PI + rad;
489|            }
490|            labelRotate = rad - PI;
491|        }
492|
493|        hasLabelRotate = !!labelRotate;
494|
495|        label.x = textX;
496|        label.y = textY;
497|        label.rotation = labelRotate;
```

Relevant local vars in the same closure: `midAngle` (labelLayout.ts:413 `const midAngle = (sectorShape.startAngle + sectorShape.endAngle) / 2;`), `nx` (414 `Math.cos(midAngle)`), `ny` (415 `Math.sin(midAngle)`), `labelPosition` (383).

Math of the current `'tangential'` branch: `rad = normalize(PI/2 - midAngle)` into [0, 2PI); on the lower half (`ny > 0`) it adds PI; then subtracts PI. Net result:
- upper half (ny <= 0): `labelRotate = normalize(PI/2 - midAngle) - PI`
- lower half (ny  > 0): `labelRotate = normalize(PI/2 - midAngle)`
i.e. the two halves differ by PI. Both branches keep |rotation| <= PI/2 (never literally upside down), but there is a 180-degree reading-direction JUMP at the 3 o'clock and 9 o'clock boundaries — that jump is "the flip" this requirement removes.

Removing the `isDown` adjustment gives `labelRotate = normalize(PI/2 - midAngle) - PI`, i.e. congruent to `-midAngle - PI/2 (mod 2PI)` for every slice: a continuous tangential rotation with a constant glyph-up direction (always pointing outward from the center). Note that on the upper half `'tangential-noflip'` is byte-identical to `'tangential'`, and on the lower half it differs by exactly PI.

